+## Built-in Calendar source
+
+The built-in `calendar/event` source uses the phone's native calendar reader and the calendars
+enabled in the mobile app. It requires the caller's `Calendar` permission and returns up to ten
+upcoming events in the next seven days. Its event IDs are positions in that list; treat an envelope
+as a complete replacement rather than merging events by ID.
+
+The `attendees` property offers `longText` with **one participant display name per newline**,
+including room/resource participants. Names are trimmed, embedded CR/LF is replaced with a space,
+and missing/blank names are omitted. Commas remain inside names; do not split on them. Email
+addresses are not substituted. An empty string means no usable display names were supplied by
+the native reader, not proof that the event has no participants.
+
+This field is included when requested in `properties`, or when `properties` is null (all fields).
+Older mobile app releases omit it. Discover `attendees: ["longText"]` in the source declaration
+using `Pebble.enumeratePlugins()` before requesting it, and check for a missing property when
+reading. It uses the existing calendar reader and permission; no separate calendar login is needed.
+
 ## Shapes
 
 A property isn't typed as "a number" or "a string". It offers one or more **shapes**: fixed types
